      "widgets_values": [
        "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Realistic live-action practical film photography. A vertical split-screen composition features two sportscasts in a high-tech studio environment. On the left, a charismatic man in a sharp navy suit with a headset leans forward aggressively, gesturing wildly with his hands as he argues. On the right, a woman in a professional blazer and gold earrings leans back, rolling her eyes and dismissively while shaking her head in disbelief. Both are situated in front of blurred digital LED screens displaying basketball statistics and glowing heat maps. The man (S1) shouts, <d>[English]\"If we let a guy who can jump through the backboard play, the game is dead!</d>. The woman (S2) retorts with a sharp laugh, <d>[English]\"It's called evolution, Marcus, you're just scared!</d>. The lighting is bright studio-key with cool rim lights. The camera remains locked-off in a stable view, maintaining the perfect split-screen throughout.\n\noverall_soundscape: The low hum of studio cooling fans, the rhythmic rustle of clothing during energetic gestures, and the sharp thumping of hands hitting a desk.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A"
      ],
